{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrbNLnhsaiA7ZztXX3J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013g6UdHpUxqgB3xon4tafLu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/engine && head -40 API-INDEX.md && grep -n \"^#\" AI_GUIDE.md | head -80","description":"Skim API index header and guide sections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5778,"cache_read_input_tokens":181808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5778},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"04bbc3b5-cd0e-48c5-9191-57e4e783933b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:11.917Z","request_id":"req_011CghrbN79hB4GSQBUQk8to","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013g6UdHpUxqgB3xon4tafLu":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/engine && head -40 API-INDEX.md && grep -n \"^#\" AI_GUIDE.md | head -80","description":"Skim API index header and guide sections"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013g6UdHpUxqgB3xon4tafLu","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\n1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"3989a700-a90f-4d95-9277-599c1cd71c2f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:11.932Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\n1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013g6UdHpUxqgB3xon4tafLu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
