{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghrcd8Zr7Jop9rp9b366","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AxhZUfa3PMTdohMAPxB63f","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"voice\\|glyphs\\|lastDevice\\|idle\\|sfxBus\\|\\.master\\|audio.ctx\\|new E.View\\|E.VIEWS\\|mouseGround\\|screenDirToGround\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Search API index for dialog voice, glyphs, audio bus, views"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11585,"cache_read_input_tokens":190698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11585},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"880fac64-3f7e-4260-af46-a326db0e279b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:21.668Z","request_id":"req_011CghrccuAdzW6Hufc2Kizq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AxhZUfa3PMTdohMAPxB63f":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/engine && grep -n \"voice\\|glyphs\\|lastDevice\\|idle\\|sfxBus\\|\\.master\\|audio.ctx\\|new E.View\\|E.VIEWS\\|mouseGround\\|screenDirToGround\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Search API index for dialog voice, glyphs, audio bus, views"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01AxhZUfa3PMTdohMAPxB63f":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/engine"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AxhZUfa3PMTdohMAPxB63f","type":"tool_result","content":"221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"57a696be-b1a9-48ae-b959-12d6a0a7592a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:21.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AxhZUfa3PMTdohMAPxB63f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghrd1snbKp4tsgQGezLf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SHNz63D1PusAhKZDR434hD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1040,1140p API-INDEX.md","description":"Read audio and dialog API index entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":202283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2303},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"c0d8cfed-ba67-4d2e-bc0a-15d3138e5e81","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:25.873Z","request_id":"req_011Cghrd1aRt5B7t5aCgWV47","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SHNz63D1PusAhKZDR434hD":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/engine && sed -n 1040,1140p API-INDEX.md","description":"Read audio and dialog API index entries"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01SHNz63D1PusAhKZDR434hD":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/engine"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SHNz63D1PusAhKZDR434hD","type":"tool_result","content":"- `grid.add(o, x = o.x, y = o.y)`: put o in the bucket at (x, y)\n- `grid.build(list, xk = 'x', yk = 'y')`: clear, then add every live thing in list (skips o.dead); do it once a step\n- `grid.clear()`: empty it\n- `grid.near(x, y, r, fn)`: call fn(o) for everything in the cells touching the circle (check the exact distance yourself)\n- `grid.query(x, y, r)`: what lies within about r of (x, y), as a list (near() calls a function instead)\n- `grid.cell`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply. cell: the bucket size in world units; map: the buckets\n\n## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\n\n- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n- `backdrop.draw(r)` †: draw the backdrop first in draw(r), before the level; it scrolls with the camera by each layer's parallax\n- `backdrop.layers` †: its scenery layers, back to front, with their defaults filled in\n- `backdrop.sky` †: the sky's gradient colors, top to bottom\n\n## 21c. Props\n\n- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(name, opts)\n- `E.prop(name, o = {})`: build (and cache) a prop: { frames: [sprite], glow: [sprite] | null, w, h }\n\n## 21e. Shapes\n\n- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id: sprite } } (sprites are E.sprite data; a color may be 'material:tone', tone deep | sh | base | lt | hi)\n- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArray, top row first, v up the tile) }; null for an unknown material\n- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and y), c, s (the turn's cosine and sine) }; null for an unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a collider\n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (distinct), pixels, bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1], rgba }; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shape draws; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three corners a triangle; uv two a corner, world units across the surface)\n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n\n## 21. Ui\n\n- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom', y, alpha, vars: the values {$name} reads } choices: ['YES', 'NO'], shown on the last page (picked by the keys, or a tap or click on one); onChoice(i) gets the one picked. update(dt) returns true while a modal box is open: return from your update then, and play waits\n- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n- `talk.game`: its game\n- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"8e8f3baf-3357-4218-9f9e-ee341dd848ad","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:25.885Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `grid.add(o, x = o.x, y = o.y)`: put o in the bucket at (x, y)\n- `grid.build(list, xk = 'x', yk = 'y')`: clear, then add every live thing in list (skips o.dead); do it once a step\n- `grid.clear()`: empty it\n- `grid.near(x, y, r, fn)`: call fn(o) for everything in the cells touching the circle (check the exact distance yourself)\n- `grid.query(x, y, r)`: what lies within about r of (x, y), as a list (near() calls a function instead)\n- `grid.cell`: new E.SpatialHash(cell = 32): buckets things by position, to find what is near cheaply. cell: the bucket size in world units; map: the buckets\n\n## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. stop() puts the music back\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\n\n- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n- `backdrop.draw(r)` †: draw the backdrop first in draw(r), before the level; it scrolls with the camera by each layer's parallax\n- `backdrop.layers` †: its scenery layers, back to front, with their defaults filled in\n- `backdrop.sky` †: the sky's gradient colors, top to bottom\n\n## 21c. Props\n\n- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(name, opts)\n- `E.prop(name, o = {})`: build (and cache) a prop: { frames: [sprite], glow: [sprite] | null, w, h }\n\n## 21e. Shapes\n\n- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets' as 'SET:id' from E.addAssets, and your own: E.SHAPES.stool = {...})\n- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id: sprite } } (sprites are E.sprite data; a color may be 'material:tone', tone deep | sh | base | lt | hi)\n- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArray, top row first, v up the tile) }; null for an unknown material\n- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and y), c, s (the turn's cosine and sine) }; null for an unknown shape. map.solid makes one solid; world.shape gives it a collider\n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (distinct), pixels, bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1], rgba }; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shape draws; null for an unknown shape\n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three corners a triangle; uv two a corner, world units across the surface)\n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n\n## 21. Ui\n\n- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom', y, alpha, vars: the values {$name} reads } choices: ['YES', 'NO'], shown on the last page (picked by the keys, or a tap or click on one); onChoice(i) gets the one picked. update(dt) returns true while a modal box is open: return from your update then, and play waits\n- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n- `talk.game`: its game\n- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SHNz63D1PusAhKZDR434hD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
