her\\|timeScale\\|mouseGround\\|W\\b\\|H\\b\\)\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Read TileMap and renderer API index entries"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011T5kgRvAF7d11HWX6NowxA","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], types, floorTex } (built in code: fill, setFloor; with no cells it starts as open floor).\n- `new E.TileMap({ types })`: types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH, face, roof }\n- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n- `new E.TileMap({ floorTex })`: floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view) -> [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, glow]\n- `new E.TileMap({ floorMat, floorMats })`: a material for the floor, floorMats: { tag: material } for tagged cells (in place of floorTex)\n- `new E.TileMap({ block })`: ['water', 'lava'] floor tags nobody can walk on (or put block: true in a legend entry)\n- `new E.TileMap({ chunks })`: bake the floor in squares near the camera (true, false; by default a map of more than 128 x 128 cells)\n- `map.arcClear(a, b, apex = 20, r = 0)`: does a jump arc from a to b (feet, { x, y, z }) clear every top on the way? The arc is a parabola peaking apex above the higher end; r > 0 also checks a track on each side of it. Jumps, throws, aerial takedowns\n- `map.block(cx, cy, on = true)`: mark a cell blocked or free at runtime (a bridge appears, lava cools)\n- `map.bounds(view)`: projected pixel bounds of the whole map for this view, { x0, y0, x1, y1 } with an 8-pixel margin (camera clamping: game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v))\n- `map.cell(cx, cy)`: the wall type id at a cell (0 = floor, -1 outside the map)\n- `map.center(cx, cy)`: the world point at a cell's center\n- `map.collide(b)`: push a circle { x, y, r } out of walls. If the body has a number z, walls lower than z + step (default 2) do not block it (it is standing or jumping above them). Returns true when it touched a wall.\n- `map.drawFloor(r)`: draw the baked floor (first thing in draw, after r.sky); walls come from queueWalls(r)\n- `map.drop(from, dir, o = {})`: what lies past the edge ahead: the first drop of more than step within reach (default 12) of `from` in direction dir, and the ground a body of its radius lands on just past it: { x, y, z, fall } or null (no edge, or a wall first). AI that won't walk off roofs, hop-downs, fall warnings\n- `map.fill(cx, cy, w, h, id)`: put wall type id in every cell of a w x h block of cells (0 clears them): build maps in code\n- `map.find(tag)`: first spawn with this tag ({ x, y, z, cx, cy }), or null\n- `map.findAll(tag)`: every spawn with this tag\n- `map.floorAt(x, y)`: floor tag from the legend ({ floor: 'water' }) at a world point, or null\n- `map.floorBytes()` †: the bytes the baked floors hold now (each view's, chunks and the lighting's canvases counted): what a big map's floor costs in memory\n- `map.groundAt(x, y, r = 0, z = 1e9, step = 2)`: highest surface under a circle footprint that a body at height z can stand on (floor = 0)\n- `map.height(cx, cy)`: a cell's top: its wall's h, 0 on the floor, 1e9 outside the map (the height rules: E.HEIGHTS)\n- `map.heightAt(x, y)`: wall height at a world point (0 on the floor)\n- `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)`: is wall cell (cx, cy) in front of what the camera looks at, so cutaway cuts it down to its type's cutH (6 by default) in this view? A game may replace it on its map (map.isFront = (cx, cy, view) => ...)\n- `map.landing(from, dir, o = {})`: where a jump from `from` in direction dir lands across a gap: past the first drop ahead (a top more than step below its feet), the nearest spot min..max away that rises at most rise and falls at most drop from its feet, stands above the gap's bottom, has room to stand, and that a jump arc peaking apex above the higher end clears (arcClear). { x, y, z, d } or null (a wall before any gap, or nowhere to land). o: { min: 35, max: 83, rise: 11, drop: 18, apex: 20 }\n- `map.ledge(from, dir, o = {})`: a ledge to climb: in direction dir from `from`, the nearest top that rises min..rise above its feet within reach, with room to stand past the edge, looking straight ahead and spread radians to each side (a gap first means a jump: landing). { x, y, z (the spot to stand on top), rise, facing (the angle climbed), edge: [x, y] (where the hands grip) } or null. o: { reach: 18, min: 4, rise: 82, spread: .28 }\n- `map.los(x0, y0, x1, y1)`: line of sight across the ground (true if nothing solid in between). It ignores heights: sight() is the one that sees over a low wall and from a roof\n- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n- `map.queueWalls(r)`: queue every visible wall box. Call once per frame after drawFloor.\n- `map.ray(a, b, o = {})`: the first cell top that rises above the straight segment from a to b ({ x, y, z } world points; o.eye and o.target lift each end): { clear, t (0..1 along it), x, y, z } where it stops (b's point when clear). It walks every cell the segment crosses, not samples; a top level with the segment doesn't block it, and outside the map is solid\n- `map.set(cx, cy, v)`: put wall type v at a cell (0 opens it: a door, a broken wall); bumps version, so caches and flow fields rebuild\n- `map.setFloor(cx, cy, tag, block)`: give a cell a floor tag ('water', 'grass', what floorTex and floorAt read), and block it (deep water, lava) or not\n- `map.sight(a, b, o = {})`: can a's eyes (z + eye) see b's chest (z + chest)? E.HEIGHTS gives both unless o ({ eye, target }) or the bodies' own eye and chest say otherwise. A guard sees over a planter lower than its eyes, and down from a roof\n- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; what stands on one sorts after it). A body overlapping its span in height is pushed out of its footprint; one coming down onto it lands on its top; one wholly below passes under. Register solids before the bodies' updates; drawing never sets them\n- `map.solidAt(x, y)`: solidCell at a world point\n- `map.solidCell(cx, cy)`: true where a cell has a wall (or is outside the map); walkable() also counts blocked floor\n- `map.standable(x, y, z, r = 5, step = HEIGHTS.step)`: can a body of radius r stand at (x, y) with its feet at z? Nothing under its footprint rises above z + step (it would collide), no blocked floor (water, lava) is under it at floor level, and a top within step below z holds it up\n- `map.toCell(x, y)`: world point -> [cx, cy] cell (center(cx, cy) goes back)\n- `map.walkable(cx, cy)`: true where a body can walk: no wall and not a blocked floor (water, lava). Pathfinding uses this.\n- `map.wall(from, dir, o = {})` †: the wall face a body touches or faces: from `from`, in direction dir (an angle or [dx, dy]), the first point within reach whose top rises more than a step above its feet. { x, y (on the face), nx, ny (the face's normal, out toward the body), top (how high it rises there), bottom (the floor at its foot), facing (the angle into it) } or null. Cells give axis faces; a map.solid box, the face back along dir. o: { reach: from.r + 4 }\n- `map.T`: the tile size in world units (16)\n- `map.ao`: contact shadow width (world units) along the foot of walls; 0 turns it off\n- `map.blocked`: cells nobody can walk on (deep water, lava, pits): legend { floor: 'water', block: true } or TileMap { block: ['water'] }\n- `map.cells`: the wall type id of every cell, row by row (index cy * w + cx; change one with set)\n- `map.chunks` †: the floor baked in squares of 128 screen pixels as the camera comes to them (its colors and the GPU lighting's canvas both), the far ones let go, so a 256 x 256-cell map costs what the screen shows; a change to cells re-bakes only the squares over them. True, false, or by default when the map has more than 128 x 128 cells\n- `map.cutaway`: walls between the camera and the floor drop low (types with cut: true; false turns it off)\n- `map.floorMat` †: a material (E.MATERIALS id or '#hex pattern') for every floor cell\n- `map.floorMats` †: { tag: material } for the cells with that floor tag, over floorMat (untagged cells have the tag null). Either stands in for floorTex\n- `map.floorTags`: each cell's floor tag from the legend ('water', 'lava', ...), row by row, or null for a map built from cells\n- `map.floorTex`: floorTex(x, y, tag, view) -> [r, g, b], the floor's color per pixel\n- `map.floors`: the baked floor images by view (floors = {} re-bakes them after floorTex changes)\n- `map.h`, `map.w`: the map's size in cells\n- `map.light`: null shades wall faces with the shapes' light (from the viewer's upper left: a face toward it lit, the other face of a corner a shade darker, in every view), or a direction [x, y, 0] the light comes from\n- `map.outside`: the ground beyond the map (ground views): undefined continues the map's floor past its edge, darkening into one color that fills the rest of the screen, a color ('#2a2630') fades into that, false leaves it empty\n- `map.shimmer` †: animated sparkle on floor cells tagged 'water' or 'lava'\n- `map.spawns`: spawn points from the ASCII rows: { tag, ch, cx, cy, x, y, z } (x, y = cell center)\n- `map.types`: the wall types by id ({ h, top, side, face, roof, cut, ... })\n- `map.version = 0`: counts every change to cells and blocked cells (set, block), so caches and flow fields know to rebuild\n- `E.parseLevel(rows, legend = {})`: Parse an ASCII level (top row first; every character is one tile). legend maps a character to a number -> tile / wall type id (0 = empty) a string -> a spawn tag; the cell stays empty and spawns[] gets { tag, ch, cx, cy } an object -> any of { tile: id, floor: 'water', spawn: 'hero', block: true } (block: nobody can walk on this cell) '.' and ' ' are empty unless the legend says otherwise. Unknown characters warn once and become empty.\n\n## 13b. Materials\n\n- `E.MATERIALS: brick, stone, rock, plank, timber, plaster, hedge, speckle, plain, tiles, slab, leaves, grass, flagstone, ... (61)`: the materials by id: { color, pattern, ...its numbers, ramp, glow } or a painter of a surface (face, roof, floor, tile); add your own: E.MATERIALS.oak = { color: '#8a5a36', pattern: 'planks', bw: 3 }. Any material id takes '#hex pattern key=value' too\n- `E.PATTERNS`: the patterns, by name: (s, m) => a tone step (-1 .. +2) at a point s of a surface, for a material m's numbers. Add your own: E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0\n- `E.PATTERNS.bark(s)` †: fissures running up a trunk; a cut end shows its rings\n- `E.PATTERNS.bricks(s, m)` †: running bond, bw x bh (6 x 3), mortar a step darker (mortar: its step)\n- `E.PATTERNS.cloth(s, m)` †: a fine weave and soft folds (fold .9)\n405:- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\n406:- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\n407:- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\n408:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hide it too (a hero lost in a crowd keeps his shape)\n409:- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n410:- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n411:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\n412:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n413:- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\n414:- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\n415:- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n416:- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\n417:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n422:- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n425:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\n428:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n432:- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n434:- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\n435:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n437:- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\n438:- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n441:- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n442:- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\n443:- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n445:- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\n446:- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\n447:- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\n448:- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\n449:- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)\n466:- `game.H`: the screen's height in game pixels (W is its width)\n467:- `game.W`: internal buffer size in pixels (HUD layout)\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n479:- `game.focus(x, y, z = 0)`: camera follows this world point. Side-scrollers: game.focus(x, 0, z)\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking opts.seconds (.4), round opts.at (iris and swirl: a world point { x, y, z }, which each scene's camera places, or [x, y] on the screen; its centre by default). With reduce motion each is a plain fade\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n487:- `game.note(text, seconds = 1.2)`, `game.shownNote`: a short notice at the top of the screen (zoom level, saved, ...): game.note('ZOOM 1.5x', 1). game.shownNote is the one showing, { text, end } (end in game.real seconds), or null: a game that draws it its own way takes it and sets shownNote to null\n489:- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"fc24a302-8089-4b5b-b8d8-8b181549c833","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:35:28.002Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], types, floorTex } (built in code: fill, setFloor; with no cells it starts as open floor).\n- `new E.TileMap({ types })`: types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH, face, roof }\n- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n- `new E.TileMap({ floorTex })`: floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view) -> [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, glow]\n- `new E.TileMap({ floorMat, floorMats })`: a material for the floor, floorMats: { tag: material } for tagged cells (in place of floorTex)\n- `new E.TileMap({ block })`: ['water', 'lava'] floor tags nobody can walk on (or put block: true in a legend entry)\n- `new E.TileMap({ chunks })`: bake the floor in squares near the camera (true, false; by default a map of more than 128 x 128 cells)\n- `map.arcClear(a, b, apex = 20, r = 0)`: does a jump arc from a to b (feet, { x, y, z }) clear every top on the way? The arc is a parabola peaking apex above the higher end; r > 0 also checks a track on each side of it. Jumps, throws, aerial takedowns\n- `map.block(cx, cy, on = true)`: mark a cell blocked or free at runtime (a bridge appears, lava cools)\n- `map.bounds(view)`: projected pixel bounds of the whole map for this view, { x0, y0, x1, y1 } with an 8-pixel margin (camera clamping: game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v))\n- `map.cell(cx, cy)`: the wall type id at a cell (0 = floor, -1 outside the map)\n- `map.center(cx, cy)`: the world point at a cell's center\n- `map.collide(b)`: push a circle { x, y, r } out of walls. If the body has a number z, walls lower than z + step (default 2) do not block it (it is standing or jumping above them). Returns true when it touched a wall.\n- `map.drawFloor(r)`: draw the baked floor (first thing in draw, after r.sky); walls come from queueWalls(r)\n- `map.drop(from, dir, o = {})`: what lies past the edge ahead: the first drop of more than step within reach (default 12) of `from` in direction dir, and the ground a body of its radius lands on just past it: { x, y, z, fall } or null (no edge, or a wall first). AI that won't walk off roofs, hop-downs, fall warnings\n- `map.fill(cx, cy, w, h, id)`: put wall type id in every cell of a w x h block of cells (0 clears them): build maps in code\n- `map.find(tag)`: first spawn with this tag ({ x, y, z, cx, cy }), or null\n- `map.findAll(tag)`: every spawn with this tag\n- `map.floorAt(x, y)`: floor tag from the legend ({ floor: 'water' }) at a world point, or null\n- `map.floorBytes()` †: the bytes the baked floors hold now (each view's, chunks and the lighting's canvases counted): what a big map's floor costs in memory\n- `map.groundAt(x, y, r = 0, z = 1e9, step = 2)`: highest surface under a circle footprint that a body at height z can stand on (floor = 0)\n- `map.height(cx, cy)`: a cell's top: its wall's h, 0 on the floor, 1e9 outside the map (the height rules: E.HEIGHTS)\n- `map.heightAt(x, y)`: wall height at a world point (0 on the floor)\n- `map.isFront(cx, cy, view)`: is wall cell (cx, cy) in front of what the camera looks at, so cutaway cuts it down to its type's cutH (6 by default) in this view? A game may replace it on its map (map.isFront = (cx, cy, view) => ...)\n- `map.landing(from, dir, o = {})`: where a jump from `from` in direction dir lands across a gap: past the first drop ahead (a top more than step below its feet), the nearest spot min..max away that rises at most rise and falls at most drop from its feet, stands above the gap's bottom, has room to stand, and that a jump arc peaking apex above the higher end clears (arcClear). { x, y, z, d } or null (a wall before any gap, or nowhere to land). o: { min: 35, max: 83, rise: 11, drop: 18, apex: 20 }\n- `map.ledge(from, dir, o = {})`: a ledge to climb: in direction dir from `from`, the nearest top that rises min..rise above its feet within reach, with room to stand past the edge, looking straight ahead and spread radians to each side (a gap first means a jump: landing). { x, y, z (the spot to stand on top), rise, facing (the angle climbed), edge: [x, y] (where the hands grip) } or null. o: { reach: 18, min: 4, rise: 82, spread: .28 }\n- `map.los(x0, y0, x1, y1)`: line of sight across the ground (true if nothing solid in between). It ignores heights: sight() is the one that sees over a low wall and from a roof\n- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n- `map.queueWalls(r)`: queue every visible wall box. Call once per frame after drawFloor.\n- `map.ray(a, b, o = {})`: the first cell top that rises above the straight segment from a to b ({ x, y, z } world points; o.eye and o.target lift each end): { clear, t (0..1 along it), x, y, z } where it stops (b's point when clear). It walks every cell the segment crosses, not samples; a top level with the segment doesn't block it, and outside the map is solid\n- `map.set(cx, cy, v)`: put wall type v at a cell (0 opens it: a door, a broken wall); bumps version, so caches and flow fields rebuild\n- `map.setFloor(cx, cy, tag, block)`: give a cell a floor tag ('water', 'grass', what floorTex and floorAt read), and block it (deep water, lava) or not\n- `map.sight(a, b, o = {})`: can a's eyes (z + eye) see b's chest (z + chest)? E.HEIGHTS gives both unless o ({ eye, target }) or the bodies' own eye and chest say otherwise. A guard sees over a planter lower than its eyes, and down from a roof\n- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; what stands on one sorts after it). A body overlapping its span in height is pushed out of its footprint; one coming down onto it lands on its top; one wholly below passes under. Register solids before the bodies' updates; drawing never sets them\n- `map.solidAt(x, y)`: solidCell at a world point\n- `map.solidCell(cx, cy)`: true where a cell has a wall (or is outside the map); walkable() also counts blocked floor\n- `map.standable(x, y, z, r = 5, step = HEIGHTS.step)`: can a body of radius r stand at (x, y) with its feet at z? Nothing under its footprint rises above z + step (it would collide), no blocked floor (water, lava) is under it at floor level, and a top within step below z holds it up\n- `map.toCell(x, y)`: world point -> [cx, cy] cell (center(cx, cy) goes back)\n- `map.walkable(cx, cy)`: true where a body can walk: no wall and not a blocked floor (water, lava). Pathfinding uses this.\n- `map.wall(from, dir, o = {})` †: the wall face a body touches or faces: from `from`, in direction dir (an angle or [dx, dy]), the first point within reach whose top rises more than a step above its feet. { x, y (on the face), nx, ny (the face's normal, out toward the body), top (how high it rises there), bottom (the floor at its foot), facing (the angle into it) } or null. Cells give axis faces; a map.solid box, the face back along dir. o: { reach: from.r + 4 }\n- `map.T`: the tile size in world units (16)\n- `map.ao`: contact shadow width (world units) along the foot of walls; 0 turns it off\n- `map.blocked`: cells nobody can walk on (deep water, lava, pits): legend { floor: 'water', block: true } or TileMap { block: ['water'] }\n- `map.cells`: the wall type id of every cell, row by row (index cy * w + cx; change one with set)\n- `map.chunks` †: the floor baked in squares of 128 screen pixels as the camera comes to them (its colors and the GPU lighting's canvas both), the far ones let go, so a 256 x 256-cell map costs what the screen shows; a change to cells re-bakes only the squares over them. True, false, or by default when the map has more than 128 x 128 cells\n- `map.cutaway`: walls between the camera and the floor drop low (types with cut: true; false turns it off)\n- `map.floorMat` †: a material (E.MATERIALS id or '#hex pattern') for every floor cell\n- `map.floorMats` †: { tag: material } for the cells with that floor tag, over floorMat (untagged cells have the tag null). Either stands in for floorTex\n- `map.floorTags`: each cell's floor tag from the legend ('water', 'lava', ...), row by row, or null for a map built from cells\n- `map.floorTex`: floorTex(x, y, tag, view) -> [r, g, b], the floor's color per pixel\n- `map.floors`: the baked floor images by view (floors = {} re-bakes them after floorTex changes)\n- `map.h`, `map.w`: the map's size in cells\n- `map.light`: null shades wall faces with the shapes' light (from the viewer's upper left: a face toward it lit, the other face of a corner a shade darker, in every view), or a direction [x, y, 0] the light comes from\n- `map.outside`: the ground beyond the map (ground views): undefined continues the map's floor past its edge, darkening into one color that fills the rest of the screen, a color ('#2a2630') fades into that, false leaves it empty\n- `map.shimmer` †: animated sparkle on floor cells tagged 'water' or 'lava'\n- `map.spawns`: spawn points from the ASCII rows: { tag, ch, cx, cy, x, y, z } (x, y = cell center)\n- `map.types`: the wall types by id ({ h, top, side, face, roof, cut, ... })\n- `map.version = 0`: counts every change to cells and blocked cells (set, block), so caches and flow fields know to rebuild\n- `E.parseLevel(rows, legend = {})`: Parse an ASCII level (top row first; every character is one tile). legend maps a character to a number -> tile / wall type id (0 = empty) a string -> a spawn tag; the cell stays empty and spawns[] gets { tag, ch, cx, cy } an object -> any of { tile: id, floor: 'water', spawn: 'hero', block: true } (block: nobody can walk on this cell) '.' and ' ' are empty unless the legend says otherwise. Unknown characters warn once and become empty.\n\n## 13b. Materials\n\n- `E.MATERIALS: brick, stone, rock, plank, timber, plaster, hedge, speckle, plain, tiles, slab, leaves, grass, flagstone, ... (61)`: the materials by id: { color, pattern, ...its numbers, ramp, glow } or a painter of a surface (face, roof, floor, tile); add your own: E.MATERIALS.oak = { color: '#8a5a36', pattern: 'planks', bw: 3 }. Any material id takes '#hex pattern key=value' too\n- `E.PATTERNS`: the patterns, by name: (s, m) => a tone step (-1 .. +2) at a point s of a surface, for a material m's numbers. Add your own: E.PATTERNS.waves = (s, m) => Math.sin(s.u / (m.size || 3)) > .8 ? 1 : 0\n- `E.PATTERNS.bark(s)` †: fissures running up a trunk; a cut end shows its rings\n- `E.PATTERNS.bricks(s, m)` †: running bond, bw x bh (6 x 3), mortar a step darker (mortar: its step)\n- `E.PATTERNS.cloth(s, m)` †: a fine weave and soft folds (fold .9)\n405:- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\n406:- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\n407:- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\n408:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), actors } picks the colors, and with actors: true other bodies drawn in front hide it too (a hero lost in a crowd keeps his shape)\n409:- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n410:- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n411:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\n412:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n413:- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\n414:- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\n415:- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n416:- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\n417:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n418:- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n419:- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n420:- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n421:- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n422:- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n423:- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n425:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lower one (grass, a crate, a barrel) doesn't; hides: true or false says so.\n428:- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, sprites, bodies), nothing else changes\n429:- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n432:- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\n433:- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost (the last five use the actor path), t (an E.anim's clock: spr may be one), rot (radians, about its center: anchor 'center' unless given), steps (16), scale, wrap: [w, h] (a world that wraps round: a copy across each edge it crosses; w alone wraps x) }\n434:- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\n435:- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n437:- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\n438:- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\n439:- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n440:- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n441:- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n442:- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\n443:- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\n444:- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n445:- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\n446:- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\n447:- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\n448:- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\n449:- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)\n466:- `game.H`: the screen's height in game pixels (W is its width)\n467:- `game.W`: internal buffer size in pixels (HUD layout)\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n479:- `game.focus(x, y, z = 0)`: camera follows this world point. Side-scrollers: game.focus(x, 0, z)\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris', 'mosaic', 'swirl' or 'dissolve', each way taking opts.seconds (.4), round opts.at (iris and swirl: a world point { x, y, z }, which each scene's camera places, or [x, y] on the screen; its centre by default). With reduce motion each is a plain fade\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n487:- `game.note(text, seconds = 1.2)`, `game.shownNote`: a short notice at the top of the screen (zoom level, saved, ...): game.note('ZOOM 1.5x', 1). game.shownNote is the one showing, { text, end } (end in game.real seconds), or null: a game that draws it its own way takes it and sets shownNote to null\n489:- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011T5kgRvAF7d11HWX6NowxA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
