{"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","uuid":"b3907ea3-8594-47e5-a7f4-e08094bb8e40","compact_metadata":{"trigger":"auto","pre_tokens":967551,"post_tokens":11847,"cumulative_dropped_tokens":955704,"duration_ms":99449,"preserved_segment":{"head_uuid":"4e577b74-a072-45f3-ba79-f75301c0ae8e","anchor_uuid":"5b4769a9-1cc4-4bfe-af61-f5634d5f2980","tail_uuid":"719bc013-9592-4948-9b9f-d46a5e575963"},"preserved_messages":{"anchor_uuid":"5b4769a9-1cc4-4bfe-af61-f5634d5f2980","uuids":["4e577b74-a072-45f3-ba79-f75301c0ae8e","d1f58148-090b-430e-b898-648ca2b74146","a3c8d0dd-9bfe-433c-b25d-265363736ca5","719bc013-9592-4948-9b9f-d46a5e575963"],"all_uuids":["4e577b74-a072-45f3-ba79-f75301c0ae8e","d1f58148-090b-430e-b898-648ca2b74146","a3c8d0dd-9bfe-433c-b25d-265363736ca5","719bc013-9592-4948-9b9f-d46a5e575963"]}},"logical_parent_uuid":"719bc013-9592-4948-9b9f-d46a5e575963","session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user ran `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A Stop hook enforces this.\n\n   STAGE.md: build the game TASK.md describes, following PLAN.md and the title it gives; TASK.md wins where they disagree.\n\n   The game is **Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons**, a turn-based grand strategy game with tactical hex battles, inspired by Brigandine.\n\n   Deliverables:\n   - Dev folder: `BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/`.\n   - Single file: `BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220.html` in the work root.\n   - `exit-interview.json` in the root, in TASK.md's exact shape, every value filled (\"unknown\" where unconfirmable).\n   - About/Credits in the game, and the final chat reply, both carrying Source Information, Testing Feedback (4 answers), Engine Feedback (6 answers) and Prompt Feedback (4 answers).\n\n   Source Information fields: Date 2026-11-04 05:02:20; Source; Plan (PLAN.md); Genre and Perspective; Tech; Art Direction; Animation; Audio; Online; Testing; Research; Environment \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\"; Model \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\"; Usage.\n\n   Required features:\n   - Feature-complete demo; no TODO, FIXME, placeholder or stubs.\n   - Dev mode from the pause menu, with live sliders and Reset to defaults.\n   - Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title or menus; any input exits.\n   - AI Hub multiplayer, plus the game on its own.\n   - 10-foot, controller-first UI: PS glyphs by default with an Xbox setting; keyboard and mouse feel native; prompts follow the last device.\n   - Touch-only devices: \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus a settings button; no touch controls; attract still runs.\n   - All audio in code; Animalese voices.\n\n   Security and working constraints from TASK.md, verbatim:\n   - \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n   - Testing: \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count... Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n\n   The exit-interview.json shape:\n   ```\n   {\n     \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\",\"source\",\"plan\",\"genre\",\"perspective\",\"tech\",\"artDirection\",\"animation\",\"audio\",\"online\",\"testing\",\"research\",\"environment\",\"model\",\"usage\"},\n     \"testingFeedback\": [4],\n     \"engineFeedback\": [6],\n     \"promptFeedback\": [4],\n     \"aiHub\": {\"name\",\"tagline\",\"description\",\"type\",\"genre\",\"source\",\"series\",\"players\",\"controls\",\"tags\": [3-6 lowercase]}\n   }\n   ```\n   The plan suggests these aiHub values:\n   - name \"Brigantime: The Legend of Forseasons\"\n   - tagline \"Four seasons. Four crowns. One stopped clock.\"\n   - description \"A seasonal war of monster-binding knights: muster castles, summon beasts and fight twelve-bell hex battles to restart the Wheel of Seasons before time stops forever.\"\n   - type \"Game\"; genre \"Strategy\"; source \"Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena\"; series \"Brigandine\"; players \"1–4\"\n   - controls \"Stick/WASD: cursor · ✕/Enter: select · ○/Esc: back · □/Space: commands · △/I: info · L1/R1 or Tab: cycle\"\n   - tags [\"fantasy\",\"story\",\"versus\",\"pixel art\",\"retro\",\"boss fights\"]\n\n   Testing Feedback questions: how many issues testing caught; how many were critical; the most helpful test; the least helpful test.\n   Engine Feedback questions: liked most; stuck or guessed wrong; the most important thing built myself; the hardest part; what was changed in the engine and why; one change I'd make.\n   Prompt Feedback questions: liked most; what was confusing; the hardest thing; what I'd change.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2, full edition.\n     - `E.Game({res:'ps1',expand:true})`, scenes, `game.go`, `game.advance`, `game.debug`, `game.saves`, menu items as a function, settings, boot steps, `game.start({scenes, scene, data, boot})`.\n     - `E.TileMap` floorTex, `E.View`, `E.VIEWS.board = new E.View('board','Board',0,50,1.5,1.15)`.\n     - `E.Humanoid`, `E.Blob`, `E.Dialog`, `r.actor/queue/decal/shape/prop`, particles, lights, weather (`E.WEATHER.petals` was added).\n     - `E.font.text` draws a dark outline by default; it must be called with `outline:false`.\n     - The font lacks `·`, `▲`, `▼`, `○`, `□`, `△`, `✕`, `●`; I use `•`, `↑`, `↓`, `←→` instead.\n   - Each file in src/ is wrapped in its own block `{ }` inside one IIFE; files share state only through `G`. Tests reach it via `globalThis.BRIG`.\n   - Pure deterministic sims: `G.BattleSim` and `G.CampaignSim`, with the mulberry32 state in `s.rs` (`G.Rng`), JSON state, `apply(cmd)` returning events, `serialize`, `load`, `hash`.\n   - AI: `G.BattleAI` (planUnit, next, resolve, threats) and `G.CampaignAI` (muster, march, playSeason, hourFocus).\n   - AI Hub shared-world protocol: the host's sim is the authority and it broadcasts `{t:'ev',n,cmd}`; clients apply commands in order and send `need` on a gap; the host answers with `snap`. Other messages: `cur` (unreliable), `turn` with a deadline (15 s), `over`, then `finish({standings,scores,stats,awards})`. The NetDriver runs on `setInterval(50)`.\n   - Hot-seat seats; the hot-seat turn timer; privacy cards.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder = `.../work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220/`):\n\n   **Folders**\n   - `engine/`: copy of the handoff. `my-3d2dge.js` is patched in place:\n     - In Dialog.update, a function voice is called per letter: `if (typeof this.voice === 'function') { const pg = this._page.join(''), now = Math.floor(this.shown); for (let k = prev; k < now; k++) this.voice(pg[k] || ' ', k, this); } else if (...)`.\n     - In the Audio class: `get sfxBus() { return this._sfxBus || null; }`.\n     - Playwright is installed at engine/node_modules.\n   - `vendor/hub/`: session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README, examples (unmodified).\n   - `engine-ext/beasts.js`: new module with `E.Beast` and `E.Wings`.\n     - Beast kinds: quad, drake, avian, serpent. Presets: hound, wolf, horse, cat, boar, lizard, griffin, drake2, drake4, avian, serpent.\n     - Methods: `update(dt, {x,y,z,vx,vy,facing,attack:{kind,u},hurt,pose,down,flying})`, `draw(g,ox,oy,view)` (parts depth-sorted), `drawPortrait(g,x,y,size,o)` (cached canvas; scale fixed to `size / Math.max(4, this.o.head*this.size*2.4)`, drawn at `size*.55 - q[0], size*.5 - q[1]`), `mouth()`, `tip()`.\n\n   **Tools**\n   - `tools/build.mjs`:\n     - Concatenates src in order, each file wrapped in `{...}`, into `dist/game.js`, and writes `dist/index.html` (dev page) and the single HTML: session.js first after `<meta charset>`, then the hub meta tags, the title, the splash, and the engine, beasts and game scripts, with `</script` escaped.\n     - Copies the harness files plus game.html into `dist/hub/`.\n     - Guard: `banned = { test: line => /\\b(TODO|FIXME|XXX)\\b/.test(line) || /placeholder|lorem/i.test(line) }`, and it fails on non-data asset URLs.\n     - Hub meta tags: session 1, players 2-4, mode shared-world, goal, howto, minutes 9, `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4.\n   - `tools/shot.mjs`: `node tools/shot.mjs name=hash;step;step ... [--size WxH] [--page path]`.\n     - Steps: wait, key, hold, js, shot, and `zoom:x,y,w,h` (the game's buffer region scaled ×4).\n     - Steps are split on `;;` when present, otherwise `;`. The job is split on the first `=` only.\n     - Writes `.tmp/shots/*.png` and prints errors plus the snapshot.\n   - `tools/hub-check.mjs`:\n     - Spawns `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` in dist/hub, parses the port, and checks the `<title>` is ours.\n     - Runs the scenarios `two`, `four-lossy`, `host-leave`, `server` through the harness with `?auto=1`, waits for `document.body.dataset.complete`, and reads `window.__hubCheck`.\n     - Kills the server it spawned.\n\n   **Tests**\n   - `tests/run.mjs`: the one command, `node tests/run.mjs [suite...] [--browser]`. It prints only failures plus \"N passed, M failed (S suites, T s)\".\n   - `tests/lib.mjs`: `boot(hash, {before, ctx})` (a vm context with a localStorage stand-in), plus `suite`, `suites`, `ok`, `eq`, `DEV`.\n   - Suite files:\n     - `tests/t-core.mjs`: data, hex, rules, determinism, ai-battle.\n     - `tests/t-campaign.mjs`: campaign, ai-campaign, save, story.\n     - `tests/t-ui.mjs`: ui-flow (the full input-driven first season), prompts, attract, touch, dev, audio, localmp.\n     - `tests/t-hub.mjs`: hub-unit, with a fake AIHub bus, two contexts, and a `dropEv` gap test.\n     - `tests/t-playthrough.mjs`: `export async function campaign(realm, seed, o)`.\n       - RUNS = verdance 2, solmark 3, amberlyn 4, hoarfast 4, with aiPlayerBoost 1; the candle run is verdance 2 with boost 0.\n       - Also holds the `about` suite (checks G.ABOUT and exit-interview.json), `browser:bundle` (file name, no external URLs, first script is the unmodified session.js, the tags, opens from file:// and attract starts) and `browser:hub`.\n   - `tests/scan.mjs`: a helper to scan scene-path campaign seeds.\n\n   **Source files (src/)**\n   - `00-core.js`: G namespace, `G.SCENES={}`, registries `G.def/get/has/all`, `G.Rng`, `G.cosmetic`, `G.hashStr`, `G.hashJSON`, `G.hex` (T=28, pointy odd-r), the bus `G.on/emit`. Tunables `G.TUNE_DEFAULTS`: expScale was raised to **1.5**; the rest follow Appendix A. Also `G.TUNE_RANGES`, `G.setTune`, `G.resetTune`.\n   - `01-data-rules.js`: elements, terrain codes (plus transforms n, i, B, a, W, t, d), `G.seasonTerrain`, `G.moveCost`, `G.canEnd`, `G.terrainDef`, `G.sizeHit`, effects, `G.tideOut/tideIn`, `G.TIDE_LINE`.\n   - `02-data-skills.js`: 90 skills (Wisp Fire p 12).\n   - `03-data-classes.js`: 23 classes. The Gray Knight base was **tuned to [420,200,38,32,36,24]** (the plan said 900/200/52/48/50/30). Also `G.classStats`, `G.classGrowth`, `G.classSkills`.\n   - `04-data-monsters.js`: 30 species with rig specs; `G.monsterStats`, `G.monsterFlags`, etc.\n   - `05-data-items.js`: 33 items; `G.canEquip` (simplified for ruler and unique classes).\n   - `06-data-knights.js`: 36 knights. The Gray Knight's troop was **tuned to [['minute',15,3],['minute',15,3],['minute',14,3],['pendulumwyrm',16,2]]**.\n   - `07-data-world.js`: realms, 25 castles, 36 roads, pools, 25 sites, `G.QUEST_OUTCOMES`, start state.\n   - `08-data-maps.js`: the 13 maps exactly as in the plan; `G.parseMap` (an anchor takes the most common terrain around it).\n   - `09-data-story.js`: about 50 events, `G.PROLOGUE`, `G.EPILOGUES`, `G.RIVALS`/`G.rivalLine`, `G.VIGNETTES`, `G.beforeBattle`. The v_amris effect uses `aiPeace`.\n   - `10-data-about.js`: `G.ABOUT` with source, testing, engine, prompt and credits. **testing, engine and prompt are still 'unknown' and Usage is 'unknown'; they must be filled in.**\n   - `20-sim-battle.js`: BattleSim with MinHeap, the occupancy cache (`at()`, `dirty()`), the reach cache with typed arrays, formulas, Sanctum and Shrine rules, `G.cheats` hooks (god, ohko, mp), per-side itemsUsed, and Second Hands at level 16.\n   - `21-ai-battle.js`:\n     - Multi-source BFS threats, keyed per troop turn.\n     - The attacker objective: `press = (.5 + .35*bell) * (bell >= bells-2 ? 2 : 1)` times the distance to the Keep; a Keep bonus; late attackers' knights take less account of danger.\n     - In the Sanctum: a dial pull, plus a pull toward the Gray Knight (×3 once the Wheel has turned).\n   - `22-sim-campaign.js`: CampaignSim, the full rules, the event engine (`_collectStory`, `takeStory`, `_applyEvent`, `_effect` including startSanctum, aiPeace and captainJoins), dev ops, and captures placed after capture.\n   - `23-ai-campaign.js`:\n     - Personalities (ignored for human realms; autoplay aggression 1.1).\n     - The Dominion summons 0 times in Year 1 and 1 a season after.\n     - Summoning stops when mana ≤ 1.1×upkeep+30.\n     - Quests only from deep-interior castles with spare knights.\n     - Up to 3 staging moves.\n     - `CA.hourFocus`, and the reworked `neededAtHome` (allIn mode).\n     - `CA.bestTarget`, `CA.playSeason`.\n   - `30-art-palette.js` (palettes, `G.groundColor`), `31-art-hexfield.js` (`G.Field`, OFF=32), `32-art-worldmap.js` (`G.WorldMap`; Rimewall rocks are kept 60 units from castles), `33-art-units.js` (`G.Vis`, `dressHat` colours helmets from plate and crowns gold, `G.knightVis/monsterVis`), `34-art-fx.js` (`G.FX`, `G.FXList`, bellClock), `35-art-shapes.js` (castles in 6 styles, keep, hexblock, gear lowered to height 7, etc.), `36-art-icons.js` (sigils, icons, `G.glyph`, `G.keycap` with outline:false, `G.keyLabel` with arrow labels for directions, `G.glyphStyle` case-insensitive 'xbox').\n   - `40-audio-music.js` (songs and stings; `G.music`, `G.sting`, `G.layer`), `41-audio-sfx.js` (`G.SFX`, `G.CREATURE`, `G.defineSfx`, `G.sfx`), `42-audio-voice.js` (`G.voice.plan`, `play`, `letter`, `profileOf`).\n   - `50-ui-kit.js`:\n     - `G.UI`: text with outline:false by default, box, bar, `nav(st, items, o)`, `synth(n, cols)`, List with `update(rows)` and `layout`, prompts, toasts, `confirm(text, onYes, {def:'yes'})`, modal.\n     - Tip cards were moved to the left (x=8, y=40*k), plus a footer.\n   - `51-ui-input.js`: `G.PRESET` (with a create: Pad8 action), `G.In` idle and hold tracking, `G.holdDone`, `G.tapped`, `G.pressed` (Shift+Tab), `G.detectTouchOnly`, `G.device`.\n   - `60-scene-title.js`: title (camera zoom .55, version with `·` replaced), menuRows, prologue scene.\n   - `61-scene-setup.js`: `G.troopAt`, `G.ROSTER`, `G.skirmishSpec`, `G.HUB_TROOPS`, `G.SEAT_REALM`, `G.tutorialBattle`, the setup scene (realm cards 172*k tall, 6 pitch lines), `G.seatOf`, skirmishSetup, skirmishAfter.\n   - `62-scene-campaign.js`: `G.Camp` and the whole campaign scene: steps, tidings, resolve, Command/Delegate, every panel. The Organize columns are .29/.42/.29; the banner is at x+22,y+16 and 58 tall.\n   - `63-scene-battle.js`: `G.Battle`, the event player, input, AI pacing, attract inserts, hub countdown, HUD. Troop order banners are 38*k wide.\n   - `64-scene-event.js`:\n     - `G.Talk` (run, skip, backlog), `G.EXTRA_LOOKS`, `G.STAGES`, `G.Stage`, the event scene.\n     - Cast facing was changed to `Math.PI/2 + (i < a.length/2 ? -.8 : .8)`, and the speaker's to `Math.PI/2 + (mx > c.x ? -.9 : .9)`.\n     - Prompts sit at `y: r.H - 84*k`.\n   - `65-scene-results.js`: results, `G.goEnding`, ending, credits, `G.creditLines`.\n   - `66-scene-about.js`: the about and help paged scenes.\n   - `67-scene-attract.js`: `G.Attract` (start, stop, watch), beats wheel, summon, battle, gray, logo.\n   - `70-dev.js`: `G.Dev` panel (6 tabs), `G.cheats`, `G.loadTune`, gallery (camera start .8).\n   - `80-net-hub.js`: `G.hub` NetDriver, hubOver and hubWait scenes, `G.SEAT_COLORS`.\n   - `81-local-mp.js`: `G.LocalMP` turn timer.\n   - `90-main.js`:\n     - The game: settings list, menu items (How to Play, Dev Mode, About), saves (version 2), `G.saveData`, `G.autosave`, `G.loadLatest`, `G.validate`.\n     - Scene wrapping for dev mode, `G.devBattleSpec`, deep links, `game.debug`, boot steps, and the hub start.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Startup and wiring:\n     - `G.SCENES` was undefined in 60 → defined in 00-core.\n     - `TKC = G.Talk` was captured before definition → use `G.Talk` directly.\n     - Lists were laid out only in draw (headless) → `List.update(rows)` lays out, and `UI.synth` supplies stand-in geometry, including a 3-column grid for castle actions.\n     - The banned-word check matched 'xxx' inside sprite strings → made case-sensitive for TODO/FIXME/XXX.\n     - Test circular import → split into tests/lib.mjs.\n   - Rendering:\n     - Keycaps were unreadable because `E.font.text`'s default dark outline covered the light background → `outline:false`; UI.text defaults to outline:false.\n     - `·` rendered as `?` → `•` everywhere, and the engine's versionLabel is cleaned at draw.\n     - Gallery and title zoom adjusted.\n     - Beast portraits too small → rescaled to the head.\n     - Clockwork helmets were red → `dressHat`.\n     - Rimewall rocks sat on castles → kept 60 units clear.\n     - The event cast faced away from the camera → facing flipped.\n     - The event prompt bar overlapped the dialog → moved up.\n   - Performance: BattleAI was slow (dist, reach, threats) → inline hex distance, typed-array Dijkstra, MinHeap, reach and threat caches. A 3v3 battle went from 200–750 ms to about 46–170 ms.\n   - Balance:\n     - The AI was passive → quest restrictions, staging, `neededAtHome` rework, Hour focus.\n     - Attackers lost most battles by time-out → a stronger Keep objective.\n     - The Sanctum was unwinnable → the Gray Knight and minions tuned down, plus an AI pull toward the Gray Knight.\n     - Amberlyn's autoplay was passive → human realms use a neutral personality.\n   - Test fixes:\n     - Keep test: another unit was standing on the Keep.\n     - Comment grep: strip comments first.\n     - Quest weights: no wanderer is free at turn 0 → set turn 4.\n     - Empty-castle test: Hoarfast took Thawgate first → wound Hoarfast's knights.\n     - Tutorial intro talk swallowed confirm presses → advance the talk first.\n     - The move picked an unreachable hex → try directions until in reach.\n     - The tutorial has no \"Delegate battle\" → delegate each troop.\n     - Confirm modals defaulted to No → `def:'yes'` for end-muster, end-march, end-turn and delegate.\n     - Xbox glyph case.\n     - hub-unit: added setTimeout; the gap test now drops a real message.\n   - Hub harness: python stdout buffering → `-u`. A stray server of mine was left after a failed run; I stopped it by PID after checking its cwd was my dist/hub, and left the other agents' servers alone.\n   - Playthrough seeds differed from the sim-level runs because of the tutorial battle → scanned seeds through the scene path.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Test results:\n   - Every Node suite passes: data, hex, rules, determinism, ai-battle, campaign, ai-campaign, save, story, ui-flow (17/17), prompts, attract, touch, dev, audio, localmp, hub-unit (9/9), playthrough (5/5, about 71 s).\n   - The AI Hub harness passes all four scenarios: two 13/13, four-lossy 13/13, host-leave 13/13, server 14/14.\n\n   Balance measurements:\n   - AI-only campaigns: realms fight and level to 9–14 by Year 4, and Meridian often falls, but AI realms rarely win the Sanctum, so those campaigns mostly end at the candle.\n   - The boosted autoplay player wins most seeds.\n   - Sanctum with the AI: level 20 wins about 8/10, level 16 about 1/10.\n\n   Screens checked visually: title, battle (spring river ford), command menu, dev panel, Sanctum, gallery, campaign winter map, Organize, setup realm cards, attract summon, event stage, epilogue, pause menu, results.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The `/goal` command with args: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - Several system nudges: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\" (These are not new requests.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix the results row overlap: a long name such as \"Thornback Treant\" overlaps the EXP bar. Move the bar right or truncate the name.\n   - Optionally recheck by screenshot: the event stage facing after the flip, the attract summon after the Rimewall fix, and the realm cards.\n   - Fill `G.ABOUT` in src/10-data-about.js: the testing (4), engine (6) and prompt (4) feedback answers and Usage (estimates or \"unknown\"). Rebuild.\n   - Write `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` in the dev folder. Changes so far:\n     - the per-letter Dialog voice hook;\n     - the sfxBus getter;\n     - the new engine-ext/beasts.js;\n     - the 'board' view registered from game code;\n     - `E.WEATHER.petals` added.\n   - Write `exit-interview.json` in the work root (the parent of the dev folder) in the exact shape, then check that it parses.\n   - Run `node tests/run.mjs --browser`: the full suite, including `about`, `browser:bundle` and `browser:hub`.\n   - Make sure no servers of mine remain. Consider removing the `.fetch` clone (inside the dev folder; harmless) so the folder holds only the dev folder, the HTML and exit-interview.json at root level.\n   - Final reply: the four sections (Source Information with every field; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback), consistent with About and exit-interview.json. Notes to include:\n     - Balance tuning departed from the plan: expScale 1.5; the Gray Knight's stats and minions reduced; AI behaviour changes.\n     - The AI-only win-rate targets were not met (AI realms rarely beat the Sanctum).\n     - Research: none beyond the docs read.\n     - Usage: unknown, or an estimate if available.\n     - Issues tests caught include the dev-overlay or keycap outline, List layout headless, the Talk reference, the attacker-AI stall, the passive campaign AI, the unwinnable Sanctum, the Xbox glyph case, end-confirm defaults and the stray server.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   A visual polish pass in Chromium using `tools/shot.mjs`. The last shot was a results screen after a quick skirmish, taken with:\n   `node tools/shot.mjs \"res=title;;wait:1000;;js:(()=>{...g.go('battle',{spec,ctx:{kind:'skirmish',sides:['ai','ai'],playerSide:0,onEnd:(res,bsim)=>g.go('results',{res,sim:bsim,playerSide:0,next:()=>g.go('title')})}})})();;wait:1500;;js:(()=>{BRIG.BattleAI.resolve(BRIG.Battle.sim);BRIG.Battle.q=[]})();;wait:5000\"`\n   The screenshot shows a DEFEAT results screen whose rows (portrait, name, level, EXP bar, \"+N EXP\", \"LEVEL UP! +42 HP...\" lines) render well, except that the long name \"Thornback Treant\" overlaps the EXP bar. That row lives in src/65-scene-results.js: the name is drawn at `rx + 22*k` and the bar at `rx + 90*k`. Recent fixes (event facing, Rimewall, realm cards, tips on the left, banners) are built but not yet rechecked by screenshot.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Fix the results-row name overlap in src/65-scene-results.js: truncate the name, or move the EXP bar from `rx + 90*k` to about `rx + 110*k` and shift the \"+EXP\" text accordingly. Rebuild and spot-check a couple of screens.\n\n   Then move to the completion items the goal requires:\n   - fill `G.ABOUT` (testing, engine and prompt feedback, usage);\n   - write ENGINE-CHANGES.md;\n   - write `exit-interview.json` in the work root;\n   - rebuild with `node tools/build.mjs`;\n   - run `node tests/run.mjs --browser`;\n   - give the final reply with the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections, as the goal requires: \"your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261104-050220--x7910ab-work/0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"5b4769a9-1cc4-4bfe-af61-f5634d5f2980","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:49:55.901Z","isSynthetic":true}
