{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1mQysZNNamL3qjv2Fy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UQLtWtsBNYy6X6dtyCKnrD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220 && for f in tests/t-*.mjs; do echo \"== $f\"; grep -o \"^suite('[^']*'\\|await t('[^']*'\\|await t(\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"\\|await t(realm[^,]*\" $f | sed \"s/await t(//; s/^suite(/SUITE /\"; done","description":"List every suite and test name"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2188,"cache_read_input_tokens":86564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2188},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"5d0cd9b6-89b3-4ca0-a9b5-82b13302b98e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:04:26.409Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1mQhkFh1itYnH2uYXr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UQLtWtsBNYy6X6dtyCKnrD":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050220__x7910ab/work/BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050220 && for f in tests/t-*.mjs; do echo \"== $f\"; grep -o \"^suite('[^']*'\\|await t('[^']*'\\|await t(\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"\\|await t(realm[^,]*\" $f | sed \"s/await t(//; s/^suite(/SUITE /\"; done","description":"List every suite and test name"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UQLtWtsBNYy6X6dtyCKnrD","type":"tool_result","content":"== tests/t-campaign.mjs\nSUITE 'campaign'\n'the phases cycle: Tidings, Muster, March, battles, the next season'\n'income, upkeep, the in-season yield and desertion'\n'summon: circle, cost, three a season, the summon level'\n'bind within Bond and six; unbind; formation; dismiss'\n'move only to an adjacent castle of your own, once a Muster'\n'quest outcomes follow their weights (10,000 rolls within 2%)'\n'a quest returns after its seasons with its outcome'\n'marches: adjacency, three troops, once a season, one per target'\n'an empty castle falls without a battle; the treasury goes to the winner'\n'aftermath: defenders fall back, wounds last a season, captures join a reserve'\n'the candle burns out: the legend ends in silence'\n'Stillness from Autumn of Year 3'\n'losing the last castle loses the campaign'\n'taking Meridian opens the Sanctum; winning it wins the campaign'\n'a rival who wins the Sanctum sets the Wheel'\nSUITE 'ai-campaign'\n'AI-only campaigns reach an end, with battles, and the Dominion waits in Year 1'\nSUITE 'save'\n'serialize, load, the same hash, mid-Muster with knights away and castles stilled'\n'the save slots write and read a campaign'\n'a version 1 save migrates'\nSUITE 'story'\n'every event has speakers who exist, and choices with effects'\n'every event applies from the dev trigger without errors'\n'each realm\\'\n'all good endings and the three kinds of bad ending exist'\n'rival lines fire for their pairs'\n'the babble voice plans the same syllables for the same line'\n== tests/t-core.mjs\nSUITE 'data'\n'counts'\n'every reference resolves'\n'every species has three forms and a rig per form'\n'maps: rows, anchors, room, and the Keep reachable in every season'\n'the road graph is connected and every realm has the same shape'\n'none of the source\\'\n'no TODO, FIXME or placeholder in the sources'\nSUITE 'hex'\n'center and toCell round-trip on every hex'\n'neighbours and distances match E.Grid'\n'areas: cones, lines and rings'\n'screen direction to neighbour at all six turns'\nSUITE 'rules'\n'physical damage follows the formula (no element, no Tide)'\n'opposed elements hit harder, the same element softer, the Tide shifts both'\n'a dmgScale slider of 2 doubles a fixed hit'\n'spells need planted feet; mobile specials work after moving; Charge needs two hexes'\n'the Keep heals its owner and decides the last bell'\n'a ruler who retreats loses the battle'\n'a fallen knight takes its troop; nearby monsters may be captured; monsters at 0 HP die'\n'EXP gives levels at 100'\n'an area heal gives its caster +8 EXP once, however many it mends'\n'seasons change the land: floods, ice, drying'\n'a Summer storm burns forests into ash'\n'the Sanctum: dials light, the Wheel turns, Timeless breaks'\n'the shrine counts glory'\nSUITE 'determinism'\n'the same seed and commands give the same battle'\n'the same seed gives the same campaign'\n'no Math.random, Date.now or performance in the sims and AI'\n'a battle survives serialize and load'\nSUITE 'ai-battle'\n'every map and season ends within its bells, with legal commands only'\n'the AI wins clearly favourable fights'\n'an auto-resolved three-against-three battle takes under half a second'\n'the Sanctum and the shrine resolve'\n== tests/t-hub.mjs\nSUITE 'hub-unit'\n'both copies connect, build the same battle, and ready up with no key'\n'the countdown holds play until AIHub.time() reaches 0'\n'a deadline hands the troop to the AI; its commands reach the client in order'\n'traffic flows both ways (cursors and commands)'\n'a lost message: the gap asks for a snapshot and the copies agree again'\n'an illegal command is ignored and answered with a snapshot'\n'time-up: the host finishes with standings by glory'\n'end: input and sound stop; the standings show'\n'no errors on either copy'\n== tests/t-playthrough.mjs\nSUITE 'playthrough'\nrealm + ' (seed ' + seed + ') takes Meridian\n'a campaign where the candle burns out ends in silence'\nSUITE 'about'\n'the About pages carry every Source Information field and the three feedback lists'\n'exit-interview.json parses and every key has a value'\nSUITE 'browser:bundle'\n'the single file is named as asked and has no external URLs'\n'the first script after the charset is the unmodified session client; the hub tags are present'\n'it opens from file:// with no errors, boots to the title, and attract starts after 10 s'\nSUITE 'browser:hub'\n'the AI Hub harness passes every scenario'\n== tests/t-ui.mjs\nSUITE 'ui-flow'\n'title -> new campaign -> setup'\n'setup: one player, Verdance, Normal, begin -> prologue'\n'the prologue skips with a held Circle / Esc'\n'Tidings and the opening story play to the tutorial choice'\n'the tutorial battle: choose, move, act, by input'\n'results -> back to the campaign'\n'the Muster is reached'\n'Organize: bind from the reserve'\n'Summon from the circle'\n'Equip a knight'\n'Move a knight to the castle next door'\n'Quest from a castle'\n'the Realm screen and its tabs'\n'hold Square / Space to end the Muster, then March on a brigand castle'\n'resolution: Command a battle, play it, return to the map'\n'How to Play and About open and close'\n'no errors along the way'\nSUITE 'prompts'\n'the keyboard shows key names'\n'a gamepad shows PlayStation symbols by default, Xbox by the setting'\n'a mouse shows its buttons'\nSUITE 'attract'\n'10 s idle on the title starts the attract mode'\n'it reaches every beat'\n'any input returns to the title'\n'no errors'\nSUITE 'touch'\n'a touch-only device sees the notice, and attract still starts'\n'no scene has touch buttons'\nSUITE 'dev'\n'the panel opens from the pause menu item and closes'\n'a slider changes the outcome; Reset restores the defaults'\n'the Balance tab adjusts a slider by input'\n'god mode, KO, win now'\n'campaign tools: mana, items, trigger, jump; the DEV flag'\nSUITE 'audio'\n'every song parses: tokens are notes, holds and rests'\n'every scene and season has music'\n'every sound used is defined'\n'no audio files are referenced'\nSUITE 'localmp'\n'hot-seat: two humans take turns with privacy cards'\n'a human-against-human battle reads each side; the turn timer hands over'\n'a four-seat Banners of the Wheel with CPUs finishes'\n'no errors'","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0be74ee3-a3fa-4a1d-ada4-50a1716096a9","uuid":"afab5827-d756-4ca5-bda9-05c507102f5d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:04:26.444Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== tests/t-campaign.mjs\nSUITE 'campaign'\n'the phases cycle: Tidings, Muster, March, battles, the next season'\n'income, upkeep, the in-season yield and desertion'\n'summon: circle, cost, three a season, the summon level'\n'bind within Bond and six; unbind; formation; dismiss'\n'move only to an adjacent castle of your own, once a Muster'\n'quest outcomes follow their weights (10,000 rolls within 2%)'\n'a quest returns after its seasons with its outcome'\n'marches: adjacency, three troops, once a season, one per target'\n'an empty castle falls without a battle; the treasury goes to the winner'\n'aftermath: defenders fall back, wounds last a season, captures join a reserve'\n'the candle burns out: the legend ends in silence'\n'Stillness from Autumn of Year 3'\n'losing the last castle loses the campaign'\n'taking Meridian opens the Sanctum; winning it wins the campaign'\n'a rival who wins the Sanctum sets the Wheel'\nSUITE 'ai-campaign'\n'AI-only campaigns reach an end, with battles, and the Dominion waits in Year 1'\nSUITE 'save'\n'serialize, load, the same hash, mid-Muster with knights away and castles stilled'\n'the save slots write and read a campaign'\n'a version 1 save migrates'\nSUITE 'story'\n'every event has speakers who exist, and choices with effects'\n'every event applies from the dev trigger without errors'\n'each realm\\'\n'all good endings and the three kinds of bad ending exist'\n'rival lines fire for their pairs'\n'the babble voice plans the same syllables for the same line'\n== tests/t-core.mjs\nSUITE 'data'\n'counts'\n'every reference resolves'\n'every species has three forms and a rig per form'\n'maps: rows, anchors, room, and the Keep reachable in every season'\n'the road graph is connected and every realm has the same shape'\n'none of the source\\'\n'no TODO, FIXME or placeholder in the sources'\nSUITE 'hex'\n'center and toCell round-trip on every hex'\n'neighbours and distances match E.Grid'\n'areas: cones, lines and rings'\n'screen direction to neighbour at all six turns'\nSUITE 'rules'\n'physical damage follows the formula (no element, no Tide)'\n'opposed elements hit harder, the same element softer, the Tide shifts both'\n'a dmgScale slider of 2 doubles a fixed hit'\n'spells need planted feet; mobile specials work after moving; Charge needs two hexes'\n'the Keep heals its owner and decides the last bell'\n'a ruler who retreats loses the battle'\n'a fallen knight takes its troop; nearby monsters may be captured; monsters at 0 HP die'\n'EXP gives levels at 100'\n'an area heal gives its caster +8 EXP once, however many it mends'\n'seasons change the land: floods, ice, drying'\n'a Summer storm burns forests into ash'\n'the Sanctum: dials light, the Wheel turns, Timeless breaks'\n'the shrine counts glory'\nSUITE 'determinism'\n'the same seed and commands give the same battle'\n'the same seed gives the same campaign'\n'no Math.random, Date.now or performance in the sims and AI'\n'a battle survives serialize and load'\nSUITE 'ai-battle'\n'every map and season ends within its bells, with legal commands only'\n'the AI wins clearly favourable fights'\n'an auto-resolved three-against-three battle takes under half a second'\n'the Sanctum and the shrine resolve'\n== tests/t-hub.mjs\nSUITE 'hub-unit'\n'both copies connect, build the same battle, and ready up with no key'\n'the countdown holds play until AIHub.time() reaches 0'\n'a deadline hands the troop to the AI; its commands reach the client in order'\n'traffic flows both ways (cursors and commands)'\n'a lost message: the gap asks for a snapshot and the copies agree again'\n'an illegal command is ignored and answered with a snapshot'\n'time-up: the host finishes with standings by glory'\n'end: input and sound stop; the standings show'\n'no errors on either copy'\n== tests/t-playthrough.mjs\nSUITE 'playthrough'\nrealm + ' (seed ' + seed + ') takes Meridian\n'a campaign where the candle burns out ends in silence'\nSUITE 'about'\n'the About pages carry every Source Information field and the three feedback lists'\n'exit-interview.json parses and every key has a value'\nSUITE 'browser:bundle'\n'the single file is named as asked and has no external URLs'\n'the first script after the charset is the unmodified session client; the hub tags are present'\n'it opens from file:// with no errors, boots to the title, and attract starts after 10 s'\nSUITE 'browser:hub'\n'the AI Hub harness passes every scenario'\n== tests/t-ui.mjs\nSUITE 'ui-flow'\n'title -> new campaign -> setup'\n'setup: one player, Verdance, Normal, begin -> prologue'\n'the prologue skips with a held Circle / Esc'\n'Tidings and the opening story play to the tutorial choice'\n'the tutorial battle: choose, move, act, by input'\n'results -> back to the campaign'\n'the Muster is reached'\n'Organize: bind from the reserve'\n'Summon from the circle'\n'Equip a knight'\n'Move a knight to the castle next door'\n'Quest from a castle'\n'the Realm screen and its tabs'\n'hold Square / Space to end the Muster, then March on a brigand castle'\n'resolution: Command a battle, play it, return to the map'\n'How to Play and About open and close'\n'no errors along the way'\nSUITE 'prompts'\n'the keyboard shows key names'\n'a gamepad shows PlayStation symbols by default, Xbox by the setting'\n'a mouse shows its buttons'\nSUITE 'attract'\n'10 s idle on the title starts the attract mode'\n'it reaches every beat'\n'any input returns to the title'\n'no errors'\nSUITE 'touch'\n'a touch-only device sees the notice, and attract still starts'\n'no scene has touch buttons'\nSUITE 'dev'\n'the panel opens from the pause menu item and closes'\n'a slider changes the outcome; Reset restores the defaults'\n'the Balance tab adjusts a slider by input'\n'god mode, KO, win now'\n'campaign tools: mana, items, trigger, jump; the DEV flag'\nSUITE 'audio'\n'every song parses: tokens are notes, holds and rests'\n'every scene and season has music'\n'every sound used is defined'\n'no audio files are referenced'\nSUITE 'localmp'\n'hot-seat: two humans take turns with privacy cards'\n'a human-against-human battle reads each side; the turn timer hands over'\n'a four-seat Banners of the Wheel with CPUs finishes'\n'no errors'","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UQLtWtsBNYy6X6dtyCKnrD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
